-- `untyped_event_attribute` (the owner's refusal, language.md §11.5): a
-- quoted attribute name that begins with `on`, in any case, would write an
-- event handler the page runs as script, so it is refused, pointing to the
-- typed event the vocabulary declares (11:13, 11:34). Other quoted names are
-- the untyped escape and stay legal.
import Html exposing (Html)


pub view : String -> Html msg
view text = <button "onclick"="alert(1)" "ONMOUSEOVER"={text} "hx-get"="/items" />
